 "_method": "Estimated by hand from the HDB brochure site plans (page numbers in _geometry). For each project I picked the multi-storey car park (MSCP) block outline (the roof-garden footprint, drawn as a polygon), located the unit stack labels of each residential block, converted pixels to metres with the plan's own scale bar (200 m or 150 m bar, measured on the rendered page), and took the straight-line distance from the block CENTRE (mean of the block's stack label positions) to the NEAREST EDGE of the car park outline, rounded to the nearest 5 m. _edge_to_edge gives the shorter distance from the nearest stack label (not the block's wall) to the same edge. These are visual estimates, not surveyed: expect roughly +/- 10 m (read _confidence per project). Block centre is used for the factor because a long slab block can be much farther at its far end than at its near end.",
